  "body": "Closes #682\nClaim: cloud/fb-quickwins-sonnet\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5 (cloud/fb-quickwins-sonnet)\nReviewer model: Opus 5.5 (cloud/review-1130-opus)\n\n### Problem\nA reader pushed from a link shows no hint of how many readers are stacked behind it; legacy shows a capsule with the depth before the title (`MessagesView.swift:3476-3488` @ 87fe0d1c; `3410-3440` @ 2fe43da3, `602b900e`).\n\n### Cause\n`TopicReaderModel.linkedReader` (LOT-137) pushes a reader but keeps no depth.\n\n### Change\n- `TopicReaderModel.depth`: 0 from a list, opener's depth + 1 for the reader a link pushes (legacy `navigationDepth + 1`, `:4021, :4720` @ 87fe0d1c; `follow` is the only place a reader pushes another one, the in-topic search result goes through it); a negative value is raised to 0.\n- `ReaderTitleWithDepth` / `ReaderStackDepthCapsule` / `ReaderDepthTitleToolbar` (new file): « ‹ N » capsule, then the title, as the principal toolbar item with no glass capsule behind it (as `ScreenTitle`). VoiceOver « N affichage de messages empilé » (legacy string). Shown from depth 1 only: at depth 0 the system title stays.\n- Differences from legacy: the capsule uses the app's badge colours (`AccessibleColors` badge fill/text, a theme's `unread`/`onUnread`, as `BadgeCapsule`) instead of legacy's palette tint with white text, and its sizes follow the app's type scale (`scaledFont`); the title keeps the system inline title's size at depth ≥ 1 (legacy sets it in caption2 bold); no loading spinner in the title (the reader has its state overlay); no « back to root » button (dropped by legacy at `602b900e`).\n- LOT-137's spec line now says the count is ported by #682.\n- Not checked here (Linux session): light, dark and Dynamic Type XL, and whether the bar's title slot shows the capsule without clipping on a narrow iPhone: device check on #893.\n\n### Review\nRound 1: REQUEST CHANGES (3 medium, 2 low, 1 detail), posted on the PR; handled in `489ffe2d`: ledger Source/H.1 per the GAP vocabulary, badge colours, type scale, `sharedBackgroundVisibility(.hidden)`, LOT-137 doc. No separate contrast test: the colours are `AccessibleColors`' badge pair and a theme's `unread`/`onUnread`, already held to 4.5:1 by their own tests.\n\n### Tests\n`ReaderStackDepthTests` (new): depth 0 from a list; each followed link one deeper (two levels); back then follow again restarts at the opener's depth; negative raised to 0; the label rule (nil at 0). Not run here; the Compile check runs on the head.\n\n### Ledger\n\n```gap-new\nSection: Reader\n| GAP-682 | Stacked-reader count | Capsule with the stack depth before the title of a reader pushed from a link, from depth 1 (VoiceOver « N affichage de messages empilé »). | `MessagesView.swift:3476-3488` @ `87fe0d1c` | Same capsule in the app's badge colours before the title; no spinner in the title, no back-to-root button. | LOT-137, #682 | ported with changes | port: legacy evolution (2fe43da3) | a·master |\n```\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CDvQG8jqNrseTphdnF",
