   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, cloud/review-1130-opus, round 1) : REQUEST CHANGES**, head 9ae43fbd\n\n1. **Medium**, PR body `### Ledger`, gap-new row. The Source value `legacy-evolution 602b900e (#655 sweep)` is not a Source the GAP vocabulary allows (GAP-LEGACY-VS-SWIFT.md:8). `602b900e` comes after `2440d79` and is an ancestor of `2fe43da3`, so the row should read `port: legacy evolution (2fe43da3)`. Its H.1 value should be `a·master`, not `a` (line 11; the other 8 legacy-evolution rows all use `a·master`). `ledger.py check-body` accepts the row (\"1 block(s) ok\"), so CI will not catch it, and the H.1 counts will come out wrong.\n2. **Medium**, `ReaderTitleWithDepth.swift:33-37`. The capsule writes white 9 pt text on `Color.accentColor`. Under a gallery theme that colour is the theme's `accentText`, a text colour. White on it is not checked for legibility (ThemeAppearance.swift:48-50, 306-309), and LOT-162 measured the system accent at 1.5 to 3.6:1 (AccessibleColors.swift:6-8). Fix: fill with `accent`/`onAccent` and fall back to `AccessibleColors` badge colours, as `BadgeCapsule` and `AppProminentButtonStyle` do. Add a contrast test.\n3. **Medium**, `ReaderTitleWithDepth.swift:14`. The issue says \"nothing else of the title changes\", but this one does. At depth 0 the reader keeps the system inline title. At depth 1 and more the title becomes `.caption2` bold, so following a link shrinks it. It also skips the app's type scale: TextScale.swift:73 says to use `scaledFont`, not `.font(...)` or fixed sizes. Fix: `scaledFont(.headline)` (the inline title's style), or record the change as a difference.\n4. **Low**, `TopicReaderView.swift:121`. The `.principal` item does not call `.sharedBackgroundVisibility(.hidden)`, which ScreenTitle.swift:82 uses so the bar does not draw a glass capsule behind a custom title. A depth-1 title may sit in a glass pill. Add the call, then check on the device (#893).\n5. **Low**, `docs/lots/LOT-137-reader-links.md:30` still says the count is \"a difference until #682 ports it\". Update that line.\n6. **Detail**: the capsule's fixed 7/9 pt sizes do not scale with Dynamic Type. Legacy does the same and the PR says so; `@ScaledMetric` would fix it.\n\nPaths that create readers: `follow` is the only place a reader pushes another one. The in-topic search result goes through `follow` too (ReaderSearchFlow.swift:54), which matches legacy's +1 at :4720. Every other `TopicReaderModel(` call opens from a list, at depth 0. `closeLinkedReaders` is not affected.\n\n**Checked**: worktree at 9ae43fbd; `swiftlint lint --strict` on the 4 files passes, TopicReaderView.swift is 400 lines; `ledger.py check-body` on the body; legacy read at 87fe0d1c (3475-3510, 4021, 4720) and the issue text. App tests not run (Linux). Without `depth + 1`, the depth tests would fail.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
